# d4-snp-tob: F16/F17/F19 injection matrix on the L2SN line (+chisnp=...).
# Three L2 holder states x five downgrade/keep snoop opcodes, one line per
# (state, opcode) cell, every line on its own L2 set (no interference):
#   UD  0x4000..0x4100  MW agent1 -> dirty TIP, no client holds a copy
#   UC  0x4140..0x4240  MR agent1 -> clean TIP
#   SC+ 0x4280..0x4380  LD agent0 -> client0 holds B, directory TRUNK
# Snoop opcodes (see the .snp header): 01 SnpShared, 02 SnpClean,
# 03 SnpOnce, 04 SnpNotSharedDirty, 08 SnpCleanShared. Expected (measured
# in l2sn-snp-selftest): dirty holders answer SnpRespData with PassDirty,
# clean/cold answer SnpResp with the post-snoop state. The point of this
# trace is the snpToB/snpStable response-param distribution (TLLog /
# [ChiSnSnp-FINAL]); readback refetches every line afterwards.
# phase 1: build the three holder flavors
MW 0x000000004000 1
MW 0x000000004040 1
MW 0x000000004080 1
MW 0x0000000040c0 1
MW 0x000000004100 1
MR 0x000000004140 1
MR 0x000000004180 1
MR 0x0000000041c0 1
MR 0x000000004200 1
MR 0x000000004240 1
LD 0x000000004280 0
LD 0x0000000042c0 0
LD 0x000000004300 0
LD 0x000000004340 0
LD 0x000000004380 0
FE 0x000000000000 0
